    "sylid": 13376,
    "subjectCode": "ADH301",
    "syllabusName": "Mobility Applications Design 1 _Thiết kế ứng dụng cho các thiết bị di động 1",
    "syllabusEnglish": "Mobility Applications Design 1",
    "credits": "3",
    "degreeLevel": "Bachelor",
    "timeAllocation": "Study hour (150h)\n= 45h contact hours + 105h self-study",
    "prerequisite": "WDU201 or WMT201 or WDU202c",
    "description": "This course aimed to provide students knowledge related to Interaction and UX Design in mobility world including smartphone devices and other wearable ones. In this course, student will be taught the common principles which dominates on mobile interface design in general. Specified principles corresponding three popular mobile platforms such as Android, iOS and Windows are going to be discussed, too. An agile for researching and designing Interaction and UX in mobility will also be introduced and applied through out this course. At the end of this course, student will obtain practical experience via a three phase projects in which they have to apply learned principles. A high fidelity prototype tools and paper prototype techniques will be explained in this course.",
    "studentTasks": "- Attend at least 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination\n- Follow instructions from teachers in class\n- Actively participate in class activities\n- Fulfill tasks given by instructor after class\n- Read the textbook in advance\n- Access the course website (https://flm.fpt.edu.vn) for up-to-date information and material of the course, for online supports from teachers and other students and for practicing and assessment.\n- Complete course's Portfolio with full contents of exercises and submit to the teacher 1 day after the course",
